## macOS verification update

Resolved on 2026-09-14. The Check workflow runs ubuntu-latest and macos-latest
on every push, and has done so throughout: build, the full test suite and the
pseudo-terminal smoke test. The current head is green on both, and the user has
run this version on a Mac by hand. The native ADEPT, Tears TUI, catalog and
caching work is therefore covered on macOS as far as automation can cover it.

What a Mac still has not done: attach a Kobo, transfer to a reader, or run a
packaged archive. The tag workflow packages both macOS architectures but has
never been run.

One macOS failure is on record and was never reproduced: commit fe4d5bc (item
13) failed the pseudo-terminal test at quit, where Ctrl+C is sent and the
process must exit within ten seconds. Linux passed the same commit and the four
pushes since have passed on macOS, including that exact sequence. Quit while
work is still running is a pending quit that waits for its worker, so a slow
runner and a refresh in flight is a plausible cause; ten seconds is not a
generous timeout. If it recurs, raise the timeout and print the final screen
and status line rather than only the traceback.

